#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Integral of a Trigonometric Expression Using Integration by Parts Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "207ce1bb-8bde-56c6-bc5c-bd9959f561ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{x}^{2}-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-(3x+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546321} {:answer/id #uuid "3d5bf71e-d1f7-5404-b06d-cdd7ddc9172e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+3x-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-(3x+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546386} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1d844c-2030-5617-b47c-4ad4758ca496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{x}^{2}-2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546491} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b070a4-b26f-53c6-a6cb-ac154bdd8423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{x}^{2}-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546776} {:answer/id #uuid "fd13586a-50c7-5494-a9e4-d9a877da7ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+3x-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b070a4-b26f-53c6-a6cb-ac154bdd8423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{x}^{2}-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546776} :answer-field/id #uuid "113fdcf6-88f3-5444-8636-104a1da82ce5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2a087e4-737f-55e1-b912-34c295e29547" :question/math-academy-id "q-12701" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int ({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}+3x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x+3 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+3x)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))(2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x+3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+D)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =(-{x}^{2}-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c20d1097-852b-5f82-8d60-8924f36cf4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c20d1097-852b-5f82-8d60-8924f36cf4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316208} :answer-field/id #uuid "357cc33c-157b-5cf7-bef4-4852d1fed751" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9972073a-20c3-5456-964a-3f9b441520bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-344601" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-15\\sqrt{x}+6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-4$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-15\\sqrt{x}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-10{x}^{3/2}+6x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-10{c}^{3/2}+6c)-0] \\\\ -4 & =-10\\sqrt{c}+6 \\\\ -10 & =-10\\sqrt{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$"}]}
